{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most devtools plugins observe state in one direction: app to devtools. But "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EventClient"},{"type":"text","value":" supports two-way communication. Your devtools panel can also send commands back to the app. This enables features like state editing, action replay, and time-travel debugging."}]},{"type":"code","value":"graph LR\n    subgraph app[\"Application\"]\n        state[\"State / Library\"]\n    end\n    subgraph ec[\"EventClient\"]\n        direction TB\n        bus[\"Event Bus\"]\n    end\n    subgraph dt[\"Devtools Panel\"]\n        ui[\"Panel UI\"]\n    end\n\n    state -- \"emit('state-update')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('state-update')\" --> ui\n    ui -- \"emit('reset')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('reset')\" --> state","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pattern-app-to-devtools-observation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pattern: App to Devtools (Observation)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The standard one-way pattern. Your app emits events, the devtools panel listens."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// In your app/library\neventClient.emit('state-update', { count: 42 })\n\n// In your devtools panel\neventClient.on('state-update', (e) => {\n  setState(e.payload)\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pattern-devtools-to-app-commands","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pattern: Devtools to App (Commands)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The panel emits command events, the app listens and reacts."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// In your devtools panel (e.g., a \"Reset\" button click handler)\neventClient.emit('reset', undefined)\n\n// In your app/library\neventClient.on('reset', () => {\n  store.reset()\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You need to define both directions in your event map:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type MyEvents = {\n  // App → Devtools\n  'state-update': { count: number }\n  // Devtools → App\n  'reset': void\n  'set-state': { count: number }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pattern-time-travel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pattern: Time Travel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most powerful bidirectional pattern. Combine observation with command-based state restoration."}]},{"type":"code","value":"sequenceDiagram\n    participant App as Application\n    participant EC as EventClient\n    participant Panel as Time Travel Panel\n\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → collect snapshots\n    Note over Panel: User drags slider to past state\n    Panel->>EC: emit('revert', { state })\n    EC->>App: on('revert') → restore state\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → update timeline","lang":"mermaid"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"event-map","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Event Map"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type TimeTravelEvents = {\n  'snapshot': { state: unknown; timestamp: number; label: string }\n  'revert': { state: unknown }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"app-side","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App Side"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit snapshots on every state change:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function applyAction(action) {\n  state = reducer(state, action)\n\n  timeTravelClient.emit('snapshot', {\n    state: structuredClone(state),\n    timestamp: Date.now(),\n    label: action.type,\n  })\n}\n\n// Listen for revert commands from devtools\ntimeTravelClient.on('revert', (e) => {\n  state = e.payload.state\n  rerender()\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"panel-side","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Panel Side"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collect snapshots and provide a slider:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function TimeTravelPanel() {\n  const [snapshots, setSnapshots] = useState([])\n  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return timeTravelClient.on('snapshot', (e) => {\n      setSnapshots((prev) => [...prev, e.payload])\n      setIndex((prev) => prev + 1)\n    })\n  }, [])\n\n  const handleSliderChange = (newIndex) => {\n    setIndex(newIndex)\n    timeTravelClient.emit('revert', { state: snapshots[newIndex].state })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        type=\"range\"\n        min={0}\n        max={snapshots.length - 1}\n        value={index}\n        onChange={(e) => handleSliderChange(Number(e.target.value))}\n      />\n      <p>\n        State at: {snapshots[index]?.label} (\n        {new Date(snapshots[index]?.timestamp).toLocaleTimeString()})\n      </p>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(snapshots[index]?.state, null, 2)}</pre>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep payloads serializable."}]},{"type":"text","value":" No functions, DOM nodes, or circular references."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredClone()"},{"type":"text","value":" for snapshots"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid reference mutations."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debounce frequent emissions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if needed (e.g., rapid state changes)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use distinct event suffixes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for observation vs commands (e.g., "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state-update"},{"type":"text","value":" for observation, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set-state"},{"type":"text","value":" for commands)."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"pattern-app-to-devtools-observation","text":"Pattern: App to Devtools (Observation)","level":2},{"id":"pattern-devtools-to-app-commands","text":"Pattern: Devtools to App (Commands)","level":2},{"id":"pattern-time-travel","text":"Pattern: Time Travel","level":2},{"id":"event-map","text":"Event Map","level":3},{"id":"app-side","text":"App Side","level":3},{"id":"panel-side","text":"Panel Side","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nMost devtools plugins observe state in one direction: app to devtools. But `EventClient` supports two-way communication. Your devtools panel can also send commands back to the app. This enables features like state editing, action replay, and time-travel debugging.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph app[\"Application\"]\n        state[\"State / Library\"]\n    end\n    subgraph ec[\"EventClient\"]\n        direction TB\n        bus[\"Event Bus\"]\n    end\n    subgraph dt[\"Devtools Panel\"]\n        ui[\"Panel UI\"]\n    end\n\n    state -- \"emit('state-update')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('state-update')\" --> ui\n    ui -- \"emit('reset')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('reset')\" --> state\n```\n\n## Pattern: App to Devtools (Observation)\n\nThe standard one-way pattern. Your app emits events, the devtools panel listens.\n\n```ts\n// In your app/library\neventClient.emit('state-update', { count: 42 })\n\n// In your devtools panel\neventClient.on('state-update', (e) => {\n  setState(e.payload)\n})\n```\n\n## Pattern: Devtools to App (Commands)\n\nThe panel emits command events, the app listens and reacts.\n\n```ts\n// In your devtools panel (e.g., a \"Reset\" button click handler)\neventClient.emit('reset', undefined)\n\n// In your app/library\neventClient.on('reset', () => {\n  store.reset()\n})\n```\n\nYou need to define both directions in your event map:\n\n```ts\ntype MyEvents = {\n  // App → Devtools\n  'state-update': { count: number }\n  // Devtools → App\n  'reset': void\n  'set-state': { count: number }\n}\n```\n\n## Pattern: Time Travel\n\nThe most powerful bidirectional pattern. Combine observation with command-based state restoration.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant App as Application\n    participant EC as EventClient\n    participant Panel as Time Travel Panel\n\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → collect snapshots\n    Note over Panel: User drags slider to past state\n    Panel->>EC: emit('revert', { state })\n    EC->>App: on('revert') → restore state\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → update timeline\n```\n\n### Event Map\n\n```ts\ntype TimeTravelEvents = {\n  'snapshot': { state: unknown; timestamp: number; label: string }\n  'revert': { state: unknown }\n}\n```\n\n### App Side\n\nEmit snapshots on every state change:\n\n```ts\nfunction applyAction(action) {\n  state = reducer(state, action)\n\n  timeTravelClient.emit('snapshot', {\n    state: structuredClone(state),\n    timestamp: Date.now(),\n    label: action.type,\n  })\n}\n\n// Listen for revert commands from devtools\ntimeTravelClient.on('revert', (e) => {\n  state = e.payload.state\n  rerender()\n})\n```\n\n### Panel Side\n\nCollect snapshots and provide a slider:\n\n```tsx\nfunction TimeTravelPanel() {\n  const [snapshots, setSnapshots] = useState([])\n  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return timeTravelClient.on('snapshot', (e) => {\n      setSnapshots((prev) => [...prev, e.payload])\n      setIndex((prev) => prev + 1)\n    })\n  }, [])\n\n  const handleSliderChange = (newIndex) => {\n    setIndex(newIndex)\n    timeTravelClient.emit('revert', { state: snapshots[newIndex].state })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        type=\"range\"\n        min={0}\n        max={snapshots.length - 1}\n        value={index}\n        onChange={(e) => handleSliderChange(Number(e.target.value))}\n      />\n      <p>\n        State at: {snapshots[index]?.label} (\n        {new Date(snapshots[index]?.timestamp).toLocaleTimeString()})\n      </p>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(snapshots[index]?.state, null, 2)}</pre>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Keep payloads serializable.** No functions, DOM nodes, or circular references.\n- **Use `structuredClone()` for snapshots** to avoid reference mutations.\n- **Debounce frequent emissions** if needed (e.g., rapid state changes).\n- **Use distinct event suffixes** for observation vs commands (e.g., `state-update` for observation, `set-state` for commands).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Bidirectional Communication\nid: bidirectional-communication\n---\n\nMost devtools plugins observe state in one direction: app to devtools. But `EventClient` supports two-way communication. Your devtools panel can also send commands back to the app. This enables features like state editing, action replay, and time-travel debugging.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    subgraph app[\"Application\"]\n        state[\"State / Library\"]\n    end\n    subgraph ec[\"EventClient\"]\n        direction TB\n        bus[\"Event Bus\"]\n    end\n    subgraph dt[\"Devtools Panel\"]\n        ui[\"Panel UI\"]\n    end\n\n    state -- \"emit('state-update')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('state-update')\" --> ui\n    ui -- \"emit('reset')\" --> bus\n    bus -- \"on('reset')\" --> state\n```\n\n## Pattern: App to Devtools (Observation)\n\nThe standard one-way pattern. Your app emits events, the devtools panel listens.\n\n```ts\n// In your app/library\neventClient.emit('state-update', { count: 42 })\n\n// In your devtools panel\neventClient.on('state-update', (e) => {\n  setState(e.payload)\n})\n```\n\n## Pattern: Devtools to App (Commands)\n\nThe panel emits command events, the app listens and reacts.\n\n```ts\n// In your devtools panel (e.g., a \"Reset\" button click handler)\neventClient.emit('reset', undefined)\n\n// In your app/library\neventClient.on('reset', () => {\n  store.reset()\n})\n```\n\nYou need to define both directions in your event map:\n\n```ts\ntype MyEvents = {\n  // App → Devtools\n  'state-update': { count: number }\n  // Devtools → App\n  'reset': void\n  'set-state': { count: number }\n}\n```\n\n## Pattern: Time Travel\n\nThe most powerful bidirectional pattern. Combine observation with command-based state restoration.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant App as Application\n    participant EC as EventClient\n    participant Panel as Time Travel Panel\n\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → collect snapshots\n    Note over Panel: User drags slider to past state\n    Panel->>EC: emit('revert', { state })\n    EC->>App: on('revert') → restore state\n    App->>EC: emit('snapshot', { state, timestamp })\n    EC->>Panel: on('snapshot') → update timeline\n```\n\n### Event Map\n\n```ts\ntype TimeTravelEvents = {\n  'snapshot': { state: unknown; timestamp: number; label: string }\n  'revert': { state: unknown }\n}\n```\n\n### App Side\n\nEmit snapshots on every state change:\n\n```ts\nfunction applyAction(action) {\n  state = reducer(state, action)\n\n  timeTravelClient.emit('snapshot', {\n    state: structuredClone(state),\n    timestamp: Date.now(),\n    label: action.type,\n  })\n}\n\n// Listen for revert commands from devtools\ntimeTravelClient.on('revert', (e) => {\n  state = e.payload.state\n  rerender()\n})\n```\n\n### Panel Side\n\nCollect snapshots and provide a slider:\n\n```tsx\nfunction TimeTravelPanel() {\n  const [snapshots, setSnapshots] = useState([])\n  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    return timeTravelClient.on('snapshot', (e) => {\n      setSnapshots((prev) => [...prev, e.payload])\n      setIndex((prev) => prev + 1)\n    })\n  }, [])\n\n  const handleSliderChange = (newIndex) => {\n    setIndex(newIndex)\n    timeTravelClient.emit('revert', { state: snapshots[newIndex].state })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input\n        type=\"range\"\n        min={0}\n        max={snapshots.length - 1}\n        value={index}\n        onChange={(e) => handleSliderChange(Number(e.target.value))}\n      />\n      <p>\n        State at: {snapshots[index]?.label} (\n        {new Date(snapshots[index]?.timestamp).toLocaleTimeString()})\n      </p>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(snapshots[index]?.state, null, 2)}</pre>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- **Keep payloads serializable.** No functions, DOM nodes, or circular references.\n- **Use `structuredClone()` for snapshots** to avoid reference mutations.\n- **Debounce frequent emissions** if needed (e.g., rapid state changes).\n- **Use distinct event suffixes** for observation vs commands (e.g., `state-update` for observation, `set-state` for commands).\n"}
